model Redefines

-- Ported from this repo's own bundled USE examples:
-- use-core/src/main/resources/examples/Others/Redefines/redefines.use
-- (four bare classes, two associations -- AB between A and B, CD between
-- C < A and D < B, where CD's ends explicitly `redefines` the corresponding
-- ends of AB). This exercises UML **property (association-end) redefinition**
-- -- USE's grammar only offers `redefines` on association ends (see
-- ASTAssociationEnd/ASTAssociation in use-core's own parser; there is no
-- `redefines` keyword for a plain `attributes`/`operations` block), so a
-- narrowing/changing association end IS the mechanism USE provides for a
-- subclass to redefine an inherited navigable feature. Zero coverage
-- anywhere in this plugin's history before this.
--
-- The original had no attributes/operations at all, so there was nothing for
-- Kodkod to search over and nothing for a query to navigate beyond raw
-- object identity. Attributes and invariants below are added on top, purely
-- to give -validate a real bounded search space and to let query.cmd show
-- that ATTRIBUTE VALUES -- not just object identity -- are reachable through
-- the redefined role name, including an attribute (tagD) that exists ONLY on
-- the narrower subclass D and not on the declared role type B at all. The
-- redefines structure itself (which associations, which classes, which
-- roles redefine which) is untouched from the original.

class A
attributes
  tagA : String
end

class B
attributes
  tagB : String
end

class C < A
attributes
  tagC : String
end

class D < B
attributes
  tagD : String
end

association AB between
  A[*] role a
  B[*] role b
end

association CD between
  C[*] role c redefines a
  D[*] role d redefines b
end

constraints

context a: A inv TagANotEmpty: a.tagA <> ''
context b: B inv TagBNotEmpty: b.tagB <> ''

-- Deliberately written using "b" -- the SUPERCLASS-declared role name that CD
-- redefines -- rather than "d" (the redefining role's own name), specifically
-- to probe whether the redefined feature is honored by every part of the
-- toolchain that touches it, not just direct object navigation. Confirmed by
-- direct execution (see query.cmd/validate.cmd) that:
--   * USE core's own OCL interpreter (plain `?`) resolves "c.b" through the
--     redefining CD link correctly, including reaching tagD -- a D-only
--     attribute not declared on B at all -- so this invariant is genuinely
--     meaningful under USE's own semantics.
--   * The plugin's Kodkod translator has zero special-casing for `redefines`
--     anywhere in its source (confirmed by grepping
--     org.tzi.kodkod for "redefines" -- no hits at all; a bare substring
--     grep for "redefin" does turn up one incidental match, an unrelated
--     docstring's use of "predefined" in IConfigurator.java, not any actual
--     redefines-handling code -- unlike e.g. the plugin's
--     explicit aggregationcyclefreeness/forbiddensharing handling). It
--     translates "c.b" using AB's own independent Kodkod relation for role
--     "b", which stays empty whenever a C-typed object participates ONLY in
--     CD, never directly in AB. The invariant transforms without any
--     reported error ("Invariant transformation successful") but becomes
--     VACUOUSLY true during the search ("empty->forAll(...) = true"),
--     regardless of what tagD actually holds -- a genuine, previously
--     undocumented soundness gap in `-validate`, kept here (not deleted) so
--     it is runnable and reproducible. See validate.cmd's [translationGap]
--     section for the confirmed false-positive SATISFIABLE this produces.
context c: C inv RedefinedRoleTagCheck: c.b->forAll(x | x.tagD = 'child-d')
